{#
The answer to a bulk delete for good: take each row out of the list.

Not _bulk.stream.html.twig, which is addressed by the conversations themselves.
These no longer exist — the purge clears their ids — so the controller captures
the ids first and hands those over, exactly as _purge.stream.html.twig does for
the one row. The client re-reads the list frame afterwards for the pager and the
empty state, as it does for every bulk action.

Variables:
  threadIds  the ids of the conversations that were deleted
#}
<!-- plmail-bulk: {{ threadIds|length }} -->

{% for id in threadIds %}
    <turbo-stream action="remove" target="thread_{{ id }}">
    </turbo-stream>
{% endfor %}
